## Summary table

| Mechanism | Scheduled? | Time | Touches DB for cleanup? |
|-----------|------------|------|-------------------------|
| `internal/scheduler` cron jobs | **No** (not wired) | N/A (examples say `0 2 * * *` UTC if used) | Examples only |
| S3 presign runner | Yes (ticker) | Every **12 hours** | Updates attachment metadata only |
| Store in-memory cache | Yes (ticker) | Every **5 minutes** | No (cache only) |
| Memo/user delete cascades | No (API-driven) | On request | Yes (deletion) |
| Expired tokens/shares | No (check-on-use) | N/A | No bulk purge |

**Bottom line:** Memos ships a reusable cron scheduler package and documents a hypothetical 2 AM cleanup job, but the running server has **zero cron registrations** and **no nightly database cleanup job**. The only recurring background DB-adjacent work is the 12-hour S3 presign refresh, which is not database deletion or maintenance.
